.TH PN-SCRIPTS-ASSISTANT 1 "September 2026" "pn-scripts-assistant" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pn\-scripts\-assistant \- private assistant that runs entirely on this machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pn\-scripts\-assistant
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pn\-scripts\-assistant
is a personal assistant that keeps what it learns in one folder on this
computer, runs its language model locally through Ollama, and by default sends
nothing anywhere.
.PP
Run with no command it serves its interface and opens a window on it. Everything
the program can do is available from that window; the commands below are for
people who would rather type, and for the first run on a machine with no
applications menu entry yet.
.PP
Anything that changes something \(em writing a file, running a command, sending
a message \(em stops and asks before it happens, and says exactly what it is
about to do.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B (no command)
Serve the interface and open the window on it.
.TP
.B serve
Serve only, without a window. The address is printed when it starts.
.TP
.B status
Where the data lives, how large it is, how much has been learned, and where the
log file is.
.TP
.BI ingest " DIRECTORY..."
Read the projects and documents in a folder and remember what is in them.
.TP
.B ingest \-\-browser
Learn which websites are used. Domains only, never addresses.
.TP
.B setup
Choose the drive, the model and the keys again. Opens the same wizard as the
first run; nothing changes until the end.
.TP
.B menu
Put the assistant in the applications menu. With
.B \-\-remove
take it out again. Installed from a package it is there already, and this says
so and writes nothing.
.TP
.B drives
Where the brain could live, and how much room is left on each.
.TP
.BI move " DIRECTORY"
Move the brain to another drive, verifying every byte.
.TP
.B copies
Where copies of the brain are kept. With
.B \-\-now
make one.
.TP
.B places
The drives and folders it learns from. With
.B \-\-read
read some of them now.
.TP
.B mic\-test
Listen once and report what the microphone heard.
.TP
.B promote
Turn validated lessons into durable knowledge.
.TP
.B start\-over
Empty the review queue and let those files be read again. With
.B \-\-facts
forget memories of files in folders it no longer reads; with
.B \-\-all
forget everything learned and read every folder again.
.TP
.B start\-again
Stop waiting for a drive that is gone for good.
.TP
.B tidy
Clear self\-descriptions out of the review queue.
.TP
.B rewrite\-paths
Repair stored paths after a move, then embed them again.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/pn-scripts-assistant/data
The brain: the database, the settings and everything learned. It can be moved
to another drive with
.BR "pn-scripts-assistant move" .
.TP
.I ~/.config/pn-scripts-assistant/last-root.json
Which brain was opened last.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/pn-scripts-assistant/logs/pn-scripts-assistant.log
What happened, including why it did not start. Rotated at five megabytes,
three kept.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PN_SCRIPTS_ASSISTANT_DATA_ROOT
Use this folder as the brain instead of the remembered one.
.TP
.B BRAIN_ADDR
The address to serve on, for example
.IR 127.0.0.1:8896 .
.TP
.B OLLAMA_BASE_URL
Where Ollama is answering. The default is
.IR http://127.0.0.1:11434 .
.SH SECURITY
The interface answers on the loopback interface only, unless another device has
been paired with it deliberately. A request from a web page open in a browser on
this machine is refused: it must name this computer and come from the
assistant's own page.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success. Anything else is a failure, and the reason is printed.
.SH SEE ALSO
The documentation in the repository:
.UR https://github.com/pnscripts/pn-scripts-assistant
.UE
